{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "מקץ", :translit "miketz", :gloss "at the end"} {:he "מקץ עשר שנים", :translit "miketz eser shanim", :gloss "at the end of ten years"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Gezeirah shavah between two instances of מקץ, both yielding a count of ten years"}], :frame {:text "A gezeirah shavah links verses sharing an identical term. The word מקץ appears in Genesis 41:1 and in Genesis 16:3, where Hagar's subjugation under Sarah lasts ten years. The shared term מקץ thus signals that the 'end' in Pharaoh's dream narrative is also a ten-year endpoint, making the verse mean 'at the end of ten plus two years.'", :sources ["Genesis 16:3" "Genesis 41:1"]}} {:quotes [{:he "ויהי מקץ שנתים ימים ופרעה חלם", :translit "vayehi miketz shnatayim yamim ufaro chalom", :gloss "and it came to pass at the end of two years days and Pharaoh dreamed"} {:he "עשר שנים", :translit "eser shanim", :gloss "ten years"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "ויהי מקץ שנתים ימים ופרעה חלם", :b "עשר שנים"}], :frame {:text "The gematria of the verse phrase equals 'ten years,' corroborating the gezeirah shavah in the preceding comment: the full verse alludes to the ten-year period that elapsed before Pharaoh's dream.", :sources ["Genesis 41:1"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Gezeirah shavah between two instances of מקץ, both yielding a count of ten years", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :gematria, :a "ויהי מקץ שנתים ימים ופרעה חלם", :a-value 1600, :b "עשר שנים", :b-value 970, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? false}], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 41, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:11:00.286124148Z", :model "glm-5.2"}